w: 1.A-ri-rang, A-ri-rang, A-ra-ri-yo, O-ver the A-ri-rang Pass I go. I know not how my jour-ney will be, If it will end on the moun-tain or sea.
w: 2.A-ri-rang, A-ri-rang, A-ra-ri-yo, O-ver the A-ri-rang Hills I I go. Flow-ers are bloom-ing, a lone-ly bird trills, This is my home-land: the A-ri-rang Hills.
